    <div class="flex">

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">

            <p>In 2024, I found myself at a crossroads in my career. Many late nights were spent talking with the people closest to me about what came next and where I hoped to be ten years from then. Those conversations became a source of clarity, and over time, two things became unmistakably clear. The first was something that had been true for as long as I can remember: I have an almost comical love for an incredibly soft blanket. They have always been my favorite little indulgence—the thing I reach for at the end of a long day—and my favorite gift to give to the people I love.</p>
            <p>The second was realizing just how fortunate I was to be surrounded by extraordinarily talented people. I found myself wanting to build something meaningful with them—something we could be proud of for years to come. When I asked my husband and his sister to join me in creating Cocoon, I had very little to offer beyond a vision. There were no guarantees, only the belief that we could create something truly exceptional together. I will always be grateful that they believed in that vision and took that leap of faith with me.</p>
            <p>Today, we are honored to share Cocoon with you.</p>
            <p>Every Cocoon blanket is a reflection of the vision that brought us here: a blanket so irresistibly soft you never want to put it away; a beautifully crafted piece that feels at home in the spaces you cherish most; and a gift that is every bit as joyful to give as it is to receive.</p>
            <p>More than anything, we hope Cocoon becomes part of the moments that matter most to you—quiet mornings, family movie nights, celebrations, comfort, and everyday rituals. Thank you for welcoming us into your home and for becoming part of our story.</p>

            <div>
                <p>With gratitude,</p>
                <p class="font-bold">Madison Trathan</p>
                <p>CEO & Co-Founder</p>
            </div>

        </div>

